{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792128238,"nonce":"kk7PFGp1k67QWaESCUBLagsPS7Y=","title":"PR 189 review minors: per-host rate overrides","message":"From the PR 189 (d9b07ff) review. 1) Crawl-delay does not space the first request after robots.txt (limiter floor applies to the next reservation; robots fetch has floor 0); with an override the gap is about 0.5 s; pre-existing on main but spec/help say Crawl-delay still wins; fix by bumping _next[host] once rules parse, and drop the [1:] in test_crawl_delay_floors_a_host_override. 2) The resolve log for us-nlx says one request every 1.0s (per-host override) because spacing() reads the entry host usnlx.com, while resolve actually fetches microsites.dejobs.org at 5 s; help cites that line. 3) Trailing-dot hosts (usnlx.com.) match the override but get a separate limiter and Retry-After key. 4) IDN hosts can never be overridden (keys must be ASCII, lookup uses the Unicode host). 5) The config.example.toml hosts example is not the built-in default, contradicting the file header.","files":null}]}